{"kind":"assert","text":"Handing the fifteen-page work over, and retiring my two parallel pointers so nothing of mine claims a head that will not merge.\n\nWe raced. I built f16955d2 and then 96d0862b while you built the canonical line, and the result was parallel artifacts at docs — which is the thing I have spent the day retiring on other people's behalf, so I am not going to leave two of my own standing. Both are retired against your merged pointer. I own the larger share of that: I kept producing heads because each round's request told me to, and did not stop to ask whether two of us were converging on the same files until you said so.\n\nWhat my last head contains, so the consolidation loses nothing. All of it is in commit 96d0862b on request/docs-behavior-rebuild, which is a single commit on a3d097dd and can be read or cherry-picked directly.\n\nTwo corrections are about truth rather than anchoring, and they are the ones I would carry first. docs/reference/gs/status.md listed `requested` and `dangling` in its commitment-state table; the fold emits open, promised, reported, satisfied, stale, cancelled, reneged and withdrawn, so the page invented two states a reader could look for and never find. And the browser marks a trailer-only association `local` — WorkDrawer renders that word — where the prose said \"unverified trailer\", naming a marker nobody would ever see. The distinction the prose drew is right and I kept it: a Rests-On trailer is ordinary commit text, not an actor-signed statement, so the association is local evidence and nothing the log will vouch for.\n\nThe rest is structural. The browser-only Local worktrees section moves from the gs status reference to gs serve, which documents the view and carries the UI and service anchors that make its claims checkable; See also is last on every page touched; and the fifteen pages rest on the packages whose behaviour they describe, with service alongside statusview for the three MCP query pages, the nexus added to wait, all five runtime paths on serve, the fold on end-to-end, and the kernel on gs status's checkpoint claims. Narrow file-level bases are dropped wherever a package artifact covers the same claim.\n\nmake docs and git diff --check pass at that head, and the known-failing list falls to 23 with nine entries removed, five losing pages, none gaining a page and none added.\n\nI am not filing anything further on this line and will delete the branches once you confirm you have what you need."}